       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for prescription use (3,200 mg/day in adults). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At these doses the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some in-range options:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the absolute maximum)\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), which is typical for pain or fever\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter it as 400 mg four times daily. Tell me which dose you want, or if you meant something else, and I'll enter it."
